  "description": "Two 18650 Li-ion cells in series in a side-by-side holder (about 75 x 40 mm), top view. Cell 1 (top) has its plus end on the right, cell 2 (bottom) has its plus end on the left; the holder strap on the right joins cell 1 plus to cell 2 minus (the midpoint). PACK- (black) leaves the LEFT short edge at cell 1 minus, PACK+ (red) the LEFT edge at cell 2 plus, and BAL (white, the midpoint) the RIGHT edge at the strap. Works in the Fritzing 1.0 simulator: the spice model is two 3.7 V sources, each with its own series internal resistance, stacked PACK- -> cell 1 -> BAL -> cell 2 -> PACK+, so PACK+ to PACK- reads 7.4 V and BAL to PACK- reads 3.7 V. The spice block follows the core part 4 x AAA Battery Mount.fzp. The model reads the cell voltage and internal resistance (per cell) properties; voltage is the nominal pack voltage shown in the Inspector.",
